---
import BaseHead from '../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import ProjectHeader from '../../components/ProjectHeader.astro';
import ProjectFooter from '../../components/ProjectFooter.astro';
const experiments = [
  ['01', 'Discrete rewards', 'Checkpoint rewards and a time penalty encouraged straight-line progress, but the car failed at the first turn.'],
  ['02', 'Curve bonuses', 'Increasing rewards around turns improved cornering, but the agent still could not complete the track.'],
  ['03', 'Continuous progress', 'Each step rewarded the change in spline progress (rₖ = 100 × Δpₖ). Adding distance to the boundary as an observation improved completion, but the agent still did not finish.'],
  ['04', 'Cumulative progress reward', 'Used accumulated progress as the reward at each step, with −1 for no forward progress. With continuous controls, this configuration completed the full track.'],
  ['05', 'Vision only', 'A CNN received 64 × 64 overhead images. This configuration did not learn to finish the track.'],
];
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head><BaseHead title="PPO Autonomous Racing — Chao Bian" description="A Unity racing environment for a UCSB CS190A reinforcement learning project, exploring PPO, progress rewards, and continuous control." /></head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <ProjectHeader />
    <main id="main">
      <header class="hero">
        <div class="kicker"><span>REINFORCEMENT LEARNING / TEAM PROJECT</span><span>UCSB CS190A · UNITY / PYTHON</span></div>
        <h1>PPO for Autonomous<br />Car Racing<span>One turn at a time.</span></h1>
        <p class="lead">A custom Unity racing environment for studying how actions, observations, and rewards shape an agent’s ability to navigate a challenging track.</p>
        <div class="metadata"><div><span>MY ROLE</span><strong>Track; shared reward implementation</strong></div><div><span>STACK</span><strong>Unity · Python · gRPC</strong></div><div><span>LEARNING</span><strong>PPO · Stable-Baselines3</strong></div><div><span>CONTEXT</span><strong>UCSB · Five-person team</strong></div></div>
        <div class="hero-links"><span>Environment design. Reward feedback. Learned control.</span><a href="#result">Watch the successful run ↓</a><a href="/projects/cs190a/report.pdf">Read the report ↗</a></div>
      </header>
      <figure id="result" class="cover">
        <video controls playsinline preload="metadata" poster="/projects/cs190a/success-poster.webp" width="1280" height="720" aria-label="Successful racing demonstration with continuous controls and cumulative rewards" aria-describedby="result-caption">
          <source src="/projects/cs190a/successful-run.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
          <a href="/projects/cs190a/successful-run.mp4">Watch the successful racing demonstration</a>
        </video>
        <figcaption id="result-caption"><span>RESULT / CONTINUOUS CONTROLS + CUMULATIVE PROGRESS REWARD</span><span>Successful configuration · excerpt from the team demo</span></figcaption>
      </figure>
      <nav class="chapter-nav" aria-label="Case study chapters"><div><a href="#contribution"><span>01</span>My contribution</a><a href="#environment"><span>02</span>Environment</a><a href="#experiments"><span>03</span>Experiments</a><a href="#takeaway"><span>04</span>Takeaway</a></div></nav>
      <section id="contribution">
        <p class="eyebrow">01 / My contribution</p><h2>From environment design<br />to training experiments.</h2>
        <p class="intro">I built the Unity race track environment and spline-based progress tracking, co-implemented progress rewards and collision penalties, and participated in PPO training and the team’s comparison of five experimental configurations.</p>
        <div class="cards"><article><h3>Race track environment</h3><p>Built the Unity track used throughout the experiments, combining straight segments and different turning geometries in one driving task.</p></article><article><h3>Spline-based progress tracking</h3><p>I mapped the car’s position to the nearest point on the boundary spline, computed progress differences and distance to the boundary, and corrected parameter jumps when crossing the start/finish seam of the closed track.</p></article><article><h3>Training &amp; experiments</h3><p>I participated in training and comparing PPO agents across reward schemes, control spaces, and observation inputs, examining how each configuration affected turning behavior and track completion.</p></article></div>
        <p class="note">Team scope: training and evaluation were collaborative. Teammates also handled Gymnasium integration, Python–Unity communication, continuous controls, visual observations, and physics timing.</p>
      </section>
      <section id="environment">
        <p class="eyebrow">02 / Environment design</p><h2>Turning geometry<br />into a learning signal.</h2>
        <div class="split"><div><p>The team used a spline along the left boundary as a reference for the car’s position. Projecting the car onto that spline provides normalized track progress and distance to the boundary.</p><p>Let <code>pₖ ∈ [0, 1]</code> be the car’s normalized spline progress at step k, and <code>Δpₖ = pₖ − pₖ₋₁</code>. The continuous progress reward is <code>rₖ = 100 × Δpₖ</code>. Boundary collisions reset the car; episodes also end after two minutes.</p><p>The report describes numerical observations of position, heading, track progress, and distance to the left boundary. The continuous action space uses two values for thrust and steering.</p></div><figure><img src="/projects/cs190a/spline.webp" alt="Unity track with a cyan reference spline following the left boundary" width="1139" height="847" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>The boundary spline used to derive progress and boundary-distance features.</figcaption></figure></div>
        <div class="flow" aria-label="Training communication loop"><span>Unity simulation</span><b aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 64 12" fill="none"><path d="M1 6h62M7 1 1 6l6 5M57 1l6 5-6 5" /></svg></b><span>gRPC</span><b aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 64 12" fill="none"><path d="M1 6h62M7 1 1 6l6 5M57 1l6 5-6 5" /></svg></b><span>Python / Gymnasium</span><b aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 64 12" fill="none"><path d="M1 6h62M7 1 1 6l6 5M57 1l6 5-6 5" /></svg></b><span>PPO policy</span></div>
        <p class="note">Unity acts as the client and Python as the server, exchanging observations and actions through gRPC.</p>
      </section>
      <section id="experiments">
        <p class="eyebrow">03 / Team experiments</p><h2>From checkpoints<br />to full-track completion.</h2>
        <p class="intro">We compared five configurations, varying reward design, action space, and observations. The outcomes below summarize the course report; the configurations change multiple factors, so they do not isolate the effect of reward design alone.</p>
        <p class="intro">Configuration 03 rewards each step’s progress increment. Configuration 04 instead rewards accumulated progress, returning −1 whenever the car makes no forward progress.</p>
        <details>
          <summary>How the cumulative progress reward works</summary>
          <p>Ignoring collisions and other events, let <code>A₀ = 0</code> and update <code>Aₖ = Aₖ₋₁ + 100 × Δpₖ</code> at each step. The output reward follows this rule:</p>
          <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block" aria-label="r k equals A k if delta p k is positive, and minus one otherwise">
            <msub><mi>r</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnalign="left left"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mrow><mi>Δ</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd><mtd><msub><mrow><mi>Δ</mi><mi>p</mi></mrow><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow>
          </math>
          <p>Backward movement reduces Aₖ. Stopping or moving backward overrides the current output with −1; that penalty and collision penalties are not added to Aₖ. The accumulator resets to zero each episode. Progress differences account for crossing the spline’s start/end seam.</p>
          <p>“Cumulative” refers to accumulated progress, rather than the sum of all rewards previously output. PPO accounts for future rewards under both configurations.</p>
        </details>
        <div class="experiments">{experiments.map(([number, title, description]) => <article class:list={{success: number === '04'}}><span class="number">{number}</span><div><h3>{title}</h3><p>{description}</p></div>{number === '04' && <span class="badge">Full track completed</span>}</article>)}</div>
        <div class="split vision"><figure><img src="/projects/cs190a/vision.webp" alt="Simplified overhead visual observation with distinct colors for the car, road, and background" loading="lazy" /><figcaption>For the vision experiment, the scene used flat colors and an orientation marker above the car.</figcaption></figure><div><h3>A harder observation problem</h3><p>The vision-only experiment replaced numerical features with a 64 × 64 image centered on the car. Even with simplified scene colors, the CNN policy did not complete the track within the reported experiments.</p></div></div>
      </section>
      <section id="takeaway" class="reflection"><p class="eyebrow">04 / Takeaway</p><h2>The environment is part<br />of the learning system.</h2><p class="intro">This project connected my experience building interactive 3D environments with reinforcement learning. Track geometry, progress measurements, and collision feedback all influence the behavior an agent can learn.</p><p>Our strongest reported configuration combined continuous controls with cumulative progress rewards and completed the track. The result offers a useful direction for further experiments with more controlled comparisons across reward schemes and observations.</p></section>
    </main>
    <ProjectFooter />
  </body>
</html>
<style>
  :global(*){box-sizing:border-box}
  :global(html){scroll-behavior:smooth;scroll-padding-top:85px}
  :global(body){background:#f3f1eb;color:#272b26;font-family:var(--font-atkinson),sans-serif;font-size:16px;line-height:1.65}
  main{width:100%;max-width:none;padding:0;margin:0}
  .hero,.cover,section{width:min(1200px,calc(100% - 96px));margin-inline:auto;min-width:0}
  a{color:inherit;text-underline-offset:5px}a:hover{color:#6c7845}a:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #a0b16b;outline-offset:6px}
  .hero{padding:56px 0 0}.kicker{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;color:#73796a;margin-bottom:38px}
  .kicker,.eyebrow,.metadata span,.number,figcaption,.badge{font-family:monospace;font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.09em;font-weight:400}
  h1,h2,h3{color:inherit;font-weight:400}h1{font-size:clamp(56px,8.3vw,112px);line-height:1;letter-spacing:-.065em;margin:0 0 35px}h1 span{display:block;color:#849064;font-size:.57em;letter-spacing:-.05em;margin-top:16px}
  h2{font-size:clamp(36px,4.5vw,64px);line-height:1.08;letter-spacing:-.045em;margin:0 0 28px}h3{font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;margin:0 0 13px}
  p{margin:0 0 22px;color:#62675c}.lead{max-width:660px;font-size:18px}.intro{max-width:800px;font-size:17px}.eyebrow{color:#72834e;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:25px}
  .metadata{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,minmax(0,1fr));gap:24px;padding:24px 0;margin-top:35px;border-block:1px solid #d4d5c8}.metadata div{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:10px}.metadata span{font-size:10px;color:#72834e}.metadata strong{font-size:14px;font-weight:400}
  .hero-links{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;padding:25px 0 36px;font-size:12px;color:#62675c}.hero-links a{color:#333b2d}
  figure{margin:0;min-width:0}figure img,figure video{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;border-radius:0}figcaption{font-size:10px;color:#757a6b;line-height:1.7;margin-top:16px}
  .cover{background:#151713;padding:32px 8% 18px;margin-bottom:50px}.cover img,.cover video{max-height:580px;object-fit:contain}.cover{scroll-margin-top:85px}#experiments code{background:#333d2b;color:#d5e2bc;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.cover figcaption{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:15px;color:#a6ab99;margin-top:22px}
  .chapter-nav{position:sticky;top:0;z-index:5;background:#f3f1ebed;backdrop-filter:blur(12px);border-block:1px solid #d4d5c8}.chapter-nav>div{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:28px;overflow:auto;width:min(1200px,calc(100% - 96px));margin:auto;padding-block:18px}.chapter-nav a{white-space:nowrap;font-size:12px;text-decoration:none}.chapter-nav span{font-family:monospace;color:#929b7f;margin-right:12px}
  section{padding:96px 0;border-bottom:1px solid #d4d5c8;scroll-margin-top:24px}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:40px;margin:45px 0 30px}.cards article{border-top:1px solid #bec6af;padding-top:24px}.cards h3{font-size:19px}.cards p{font-size:14px}.note{font-size:12px;color:#848a79;max-width:900px}
  .split{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:90px;align-items:center}.split>*{min-width:0}.split figure{padding:25px;background:#e8e9df}.split p{font-size:15px}code{font-family:monospace;font-size:14px;background:#e6e7dd;color:#48583a;border-radius:0}
  .flow{display:grid;grid-template-columns:auto 48px auto 48px auto 48px auto;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;gap:16px;padding:24px;margin:40px 0 18px;border-block:1px solid #cfd3c3;background:#e8e9df;font-family:monospace;font-size:12px;color:#657a42}.flow span{text-align:center;min-width:0}.flow b{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;color:#72834e}.flow svg{display:block;width:48px;height:12px;overflow:visible}.flow svg path{stroke:#72834e;stroke-width:1.5;stroke-linecap:round;stroke-linejoin:round}

  #experiments{width:100%;background:#22271f;color:#eceee4;padding-inline:max(48px,calc((100% - 1200px)/2));border:0}#experiments p{color:#b5bba9}#experiments .eyebrow{color:#b4c68d}
  details{max-width:800px;margin:24px 0 32px;border-block:1px solid #48503e;padding:16px 0}summary{cursor:pointer;font-size:14px;color:#d5e2bc}details p{font-size:14px;margin:18px 0 0}math{font-size:20px;margin:20px 0;text-align:left}
  .experiments{margin:45px 0 55px}.experiments article{display:grid;grid-template-columns:40px 1fr auto;gap:25px;padding:28px 20px;border-top:1px solid #48503e}.number{color:#b4c68d}.experiments h3{font-size:20px}.experiments p{font-size:14px;max-width:750px;margin:0}.success{background:#333d2b}.badge{font-size:10px;color:#bdd395;align-self:start;padding:7px 0;white-space:nowrap}.vision figure{background:#151713}.vision figcaption{color:#a6ab99}.vision h3{font-size:26px}
  .reflection{border:0;max-width:1200px}.reflection .intro{font-size:26px;line-height:1.5;color:#404a36;letter-spacing:-.02em}.reflection>p:last-child{max-width:800px}
  .skip{position:absolute;top:-100px;left:20px;background:white;padding:12px;z-index:20}.skip:focus{top:10px}
  @media(min-width:601px) and (max-width:900px){.flow{grid-template-columns:auto 32px auto 32px auto 32px auto;gap:8px;padding-inline:12px;font-size:11px}.flow svg{width:32px}}
  @media(max-width:900px){.hero,.cover,section,.chapter-nav>div{width:calc(100% - 48px)}.split{gap:40px}.cards{gap:24px}#experiments{padding-inline:24px}.kicker{font-size:10px}}
  @media(max-width:600px){.hero,.cover,section,.chapter-nav>div{width:calc(100% - 36px)}.hero{padding-top:35px}.kicker{font-size:9px;margin-bottom:30px;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px}h1{font-size:clamp(42px,10vw,58px)}h1 span{font-size:32px;line-height:1.1}h2{font-size:39px}.lead,.intro{font-size:16px}.metadata{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:24px 18px}.hero-links{flex-direction:column;gap:12px}.cover{padding:15px 10px}.cover figcaption{display:block;font-size:8px}.cover figcaption span{display:block}.chapter-nav a{font-size:11px}section{padding-block:60px}.cards,.split{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:24px}.cards{margin-top:30px}.cards p{margin-bottom:0}.split figure{padding:15px}.flow{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:10px;padding:24px 18px;font-size:12px}.flow b{height:36px}.flow svg{width:36px;transform:rotate(90deg)}#experiments{padding-inline:18px}.experiments article{grid-template-columns:24px 1fr;gap:14px;padding:24px 12px}.badge{grid-column:2;padding:0}.reflection .intro{font-size:22px}}
  @media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){:global(html){scroll-behavior:auto}}
  @media print{:global(body){background:#fff;font-size:10pt}.skip,.chapter-nav{display:none}.hero,.cover,section{width:100%}.hero{padding-top:24pt}h1{font-size:44pt}h2{font-size:30pt}section{padding-block:28pt}.cover img{max-height:90mm}.cards,.split{gap:20pt}.experiments article,figure,.cards article{break-inside:avoid}#experiments{background:white;color:#272b26;padding-inline:0}#experiments p{color:#62675c}.success{background:#e8e9df}.number,.badge,#experiments .eyebrow{color:#657a42}.vision figure{background:#e8e9df}.reflection .intro{font-size:16pt}}
</style>
